{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3105","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3105","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3105\",\"parent_revision\":\"e4149b3ffe02cab9023796419da838bc80ba6278\",\"root_revision\":\"fc2a9a4319aa0e925c024e3979d86b567c0baeaecb4fb6c52d9b8171622b7483\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item \u2014 its deliverable is an experiment result or design decision with evidence (a prototype on a real plan, a measured comparison, or a written design verdict), not a mandate to ship a feature.\\n\\nOrigin: mined from the golden-path task-category discussion.\\n\\nShared design constraint (same as #3097\u2013#3103): the model keeps the judgment but writes it down once, as typed data, at planning time; the mechanical consequence is applied deterministically by machinery that already exists. No new scheduler, no generic graph runtime \u2014 out of scope.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore measuring and vetting the skill/agent discovery pass-through to task-workers** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: golden-path task-category discussion\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Why\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nDH's current flexibility mechanism: during its steps, agents discover locally installed skills and specialized plugins relevant to the task and pass them through to the task-worker (via the task's agent field -> profile_load, and skill lists in task metadata), so a user only needs to install skills/plugins and DH wires them in. By the author's own assessment this \\\"felt like a good idea and is what is currently in place\\\" \u2014 there is no measurement of whether it actually improves outcomes. Separately, this mechanism is an unvetted injection channel: discovered third-party skill and profile text flows directly into task-worker context, and injected profile content was one of the unproven-but-live hypothesis candidates for role derailment in the #3060 over-orchestration incident.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nDH's current flexibility mechanism: during its steps, agents discover locally installed skills and specialized plugins relevant to the task and pass them through to the task-worker (via the task's agent field -> profile_load, and skill lists in task metadata), so a user only needs to install skills/plugins and DH wires them in. By the author's own assessment this \\\"felt like a good idea and is what is currently in place\\\" \u2014 there is no measurement of whether it actually improves outcomes. Separately, this mechanism is an unvetted injection channel: discovered third-party skill and profile text flows directly into task-worker context, and injected profile content was one of the unproven-but-live hypothesis candidates for role derailment in the #3060 over-orchestration incident.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Mitigates\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFlying blind on a core mechanism (no effectiveness data); the incident-adjacent unvetted-content risk (injected text that can contradict or derail the assigned role).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefit Lands In\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nEvidence-based iteration on the pass-through design; a defined trust model for injected content; incident-class risk reduction.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nEvidence-based iteration on the pass-through design; a defined trust model for injected content; incident-class risk reduction.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Proposed Exploration\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n1. Define what \\\"the pass-through worked\\\" means \u2014 candidate metrics: task success rate, re-dispatch/retry count, review findings per task, token cost, downstream rework \u2014 measured with pass-through active vs inactive on comparable tasks.\\n2. Instrument the dispatch path to record which profiles/skills were discovered and injected per task (so effectiveness is attributable).\\n3. Run the comparison on at least one real plan per arm.\\n4. Separately assess the injection surface: enumerate what discovered profile/skill text can instruct a task-worker to do, and define a two-tier trust model \u2014 curated (pinned by a golden-path template or explicitly listed in the plan) vs discovered-at-runtime (requires vetting: at minimum, a check that injected text does not contain dispatch/coordination instructions that conflict with the task's declared executor type per #3100).\\n5. Write the verdict: keep as-is, keep with vetting, or restructure.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n1. Define what \\\"the pass-through worked\\\" means \u2014 candidate metrics: task success rate, re-dispatch/retry count, review findings per task, token cost, downstream rework \u2014 measured with pass-through active vs inactive on comparable tasks.\\n2. Instrument the dispatch path to record which profiles/skills were discovered and injected per task (so effectiveness is attributable).\\n3. Run the comparison on at least one real plan per arm.\\n4. Separately assess the injection surface: enumerate what discovered profile/skill text can instruct a task-worker to do, and define a two-tier trust model \u2014 curated (pinned by a golden-path template or explicitly listed in the plan) vs discovered-at-runtime (requires vetting: at minimum, a check that injected text does not contain dispatch/coordination instructions that conflict with the task's declared executor type per #3100).\\n5. Write the verdict: keep as-is, keep with vetting, or restructure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3100 (executor-type declaration is what vetting checks against); #3097 (injected profile choice could eventually key off complexity); companion item \\\"Explore golden-path workflow templates for known task categories\\\" (#3104) (supplies the curated tier).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e1e971c7c4a26e192a356662009950ca48fd9444a05f144aa862c2e51d37476c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIqX2w\"}"}